e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t & {e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368536} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7cacd27-4ba3-5e7e-aff9-8222caaf14d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368534}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dd872b1f-c8f9-59db-867a-79ae79b5ab3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-334331" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡5t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡5t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" :question/worked-solution "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our case, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡5t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡5t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}=[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t & -{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t & {e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368540 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c99cda-25a5-50f2-903b-bfb1fdc5fa10" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Fundamental Matrices Using Matrix Exponentials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fee90bc1-c28c-5ef4-b0bd-63c5765116e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fee90bc1-c28c-5ef4-b0bd-63c5765116e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368542} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b0ac857-5327-5216-889b-13ad93622cdb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368541} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4c5bdcf-6cc5-55b0-87eb-4eb3b015f4db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4c5bdcf-6cc5-55b0-87eb-4eb3b015f4db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368544} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2eafe6d-de82-5312-933e-800295acf934" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368543} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25867c2a-6e3d-5246-9ab3-39cb41e028e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368546}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25867c2a-6e3d-5246-9ab3-39cb41e028e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368546} :answer-field/id #uuid "23b741fd-2f68-5d99-8191-bf8bca142f31" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368545} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec7572be-44ad-5bfb-8f15-da9f25b854bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec7572be-44ad-5bfb-8f15-da9f25b854bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368548} :answer-field/id #uuid "edab2a91-901c-5d06-9847-de5573b5f0df" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368547}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0fceb88b-91dc-5f03-80e2-15ef97ea1801" :question/math-academy-id "q-334382" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n| ${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & 5{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -5{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=5\\text{i}t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-5\\text{i}t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r((5\\text{i})t) & ={e}^{(5\\text{i})t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}(5\\text{i})t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}+5\\text{i}{\\alpha }_{1}t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ 5{\\alpha }_{1}t=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}=\\frac{1}{5t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ 5{\\alpha }_{1}t & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{5t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368549 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c99cda-25a5-50f2-903b-bfb1fdc5fa10" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Fundamental Matrices Using Matrix Exponentials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b46abe0b-0664-5ef5-a2b2-736b760f0161" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3t}+e^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368551} {:answer/id #uuid "8ead1a0f-5067-5807-acf3-573fa8e124e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3t}-e^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368552}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b46abe0b-0664-5ef5-a2b2-736b760f0161" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3t}+e^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368551} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e02ad73-6b78-5fa3-a6a3-27e8037536f8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368550} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aada60eb-b96a-5863-9188-d39799ac65f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3t}+e^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368554}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aada60eb-b96a-5863-9188-d39799ac65f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3t}+e^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368554} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6657f3b-0ad3-5e9f-86fd-284c93bbcf78" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368553}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1995d3c4-602c-5f0c-b18d-81930b27c672" :question/math-academy-id "q-334387" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n| ${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | ${e}^{3t}-{e}^{-3t}$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | ${e}^{3t}-{e}^{-3t}$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & 3{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 3{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-3t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=3t,\n$$\n\nboth of multiplicity one. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}r(-3t)={e}^{-3t} \\\\ r(3t)={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}-3t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-3t} \\\\ 3t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- Subtracting the second equation from the first one, we get\n\n$$\n-6t{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{-3t}-{e}^{3t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{1}=-\\frac{1}{6t}({e}^{-3t}-{e}^{3t}).\n$$\n\n- Adding the first and the second equations, we get\n\n$$\n2{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-3t}+{e}^{3t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-3t}+{e}^{3t}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-3t}+{e}^{3t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{3t}+{e}^{-3t}) \\\\ 3{\\alpha }_{1}t & =3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{6t}({e}^{-3t}-{e}^{3t}))t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{3t}-{e}^{-3t})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t}+{e}^{-3t} & {e}^{3t}-{e}^{-3t} \\\\ {e}^{3t}-{e}^{-3t} & {e}^{3t}+{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368555 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c99cda-25a5-50f2-903b-bfb1fdc5fa10" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Fundamental Matrices Using Matrix Exponentials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9230be7-2c4c-5461-a20e-e69c68217034" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9230be7-2c4c-5461-a20e-e69c68217034" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368557} :answer-field/id #uuid "96e95ae5-da18-5b06-a8b0-99542b8752ff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368556} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9202e141-66d7-510a-9a10-538655f1700a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "te^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368559}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9202e141-66d7-510a-9a10-538655f1700a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "te^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368559} :answer-field/id #uuid "758c0327-04db-5677-8fc3-e534e219ed09" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368558} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82f9c4e3-5a68-5858-9583-18c21a3e1b23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82f9c4e3-5a68-5858-9583-18c21a3e1b23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368561} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fbda469-2ba9-553b-b3e3-713eb9db8faa" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368560} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b920bda-1dd4-5194-abf2-7a9da42619a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b920bda-1dd4-5194-abf2-7a9da42619a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368563} :answer-field/id #uuid "558d8559-ed04-5b67-9d2c-6f4c73a070b5" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368562}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f6832ec-b78d-5fbd-8a7b-80d82c69a785" :question/math-academy-id "q-334499" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n| ${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & {\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 0 & 5{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The only eigenvalue of $At$ is \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=5t\n$$\n\nof multiplicity two. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}r(5t)={e}^{5t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(5t)={e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}5t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{5t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{5t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first one, we get\n\n$$\n5t{e}^{5t}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{5t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{5t}(1-5t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =5{e}^{5t}t+{e}^{5t}(1-5t) \\\\  & ={e}^{5t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}t & ={e}^{5t}t \\\\  & =t{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368564 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0aea7503-74d6-5ba4-9411-ee53e59512d0" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Properties of a Fundamental Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "174e3e1e-1363-5ec8-a06f-f2095ad1b1a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Φ(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368566} {:answer/id #uuid "647dc60b-9519-5b74-9f4d-9709c601ec9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Φ}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368567} {:answer/id #uuid "5f001e02-20a1-5a36-9cce-0a0d8b7594cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368568} {:answer/id #uuid "6f63b778-b7dc-5d66-ab9d-9fc9613d6b21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368569}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "174e3e1e-1363-5ec8-a06f-f2095ad1b1a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Φ(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368566} :answer-field/id #uuid "04f57b00-0894-5466-aa31-c4b7cd702de7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368565} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17caa997-2a02-5e36-bdfe-9d6b1f0b4a6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${Φ}^{′}=A\\,Φ$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368571} {:answer/id #uuid "b4320b5f-af1a-502f-8b44-f0242645f06b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "properties of invertible matrices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368572} {:answer/id #uuid "c9ad7eca-ca21-5734-80db-7e5bec56e722" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368573} {:answer/id #uuid "735eb4db-8408-5ffc-91af-4c59237835d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9ad7eca-ca21-5734-80db-7e5bec56e722" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368573} :answer-field/id #uuid "804e3c63-8b5c-5cba-b904-c15a71e0959a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368570} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ad418af-a8a4-5016-83aa-569d6cd9e84a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${Φ}^{′}=A\\,Φ$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368576} {:answer/id #uuid "cd07a5ee-1e8a-5151-96e1-d91294ffeef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "properties of invertible matrices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368577} {:answer/id #uuid "04c013f7-4a21-51e8-aa4c-e40669ccc62e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368578} {:answer/id #uuid "63bf7436-afaf-5eee-b3e0-8e2440db6646" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd07a5ee-1e8a-5151-96e1-d91294ffeef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "properties of invertible matrices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368577} :answer-field/id #uuid "e80e6d4a-bb61-54c9-8306-e898f98e1b96" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368575}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b44d1fb2-d7c8-55d2-b679-198d5cddb501" :question/math-academy-id "q-336093" :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that $Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$ is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ be the columns of $Φ(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are linearly independent for all $t$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $det(Φ(t))\\ne 0$ for all $t$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ states the independence of the columns of {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line $\\text{L3}$ by the {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first interpret line $\\text{L2}.$ Line $\\text{L2}$ states that the two columns of $Φ(t)$ are linearly independent, which is required of a fundamental matrix. Thus, $\\text{L2}$ states independence of the columns of $Φ(t).$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of the solution space for our system. Thus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Recall that a square matrix is invertible when its determinant is nonzero. Since in $\\text{L3}$ we have that $det(Φ(t))\\ne 0$ for all $t,$ it follows that $Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t.$ Thus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ by the $\\text{properties of invertible matrices}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368580 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0aea7503-74d6-5ba4-9411-ee53e59512d0" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Properties of a Fundamental Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62054700-d24d-5d67-8f7e-e60a1a15e65f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368582} {:answer/id #uuid "36698872-b453-5037-910c-a8e0982ddc53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368583} {:answer/id #uuid "e263670a-abdd-5e7e-8183-50800969020d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368584}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62054700-d24d-5d67-8f7e-e60a1a15e65f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368582} :answer-field/id #uuid "13cf202b-91a6-5232-a463-b56b190ca724" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368581} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cc5454a-a5f1-52c1-8182-610adbb87eaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating the given system" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368586} {:answer/id #uuid "4bb6c4e4-aadf-58f8-9cb9-6e2981f11ce9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying $Φ(t)$ with it's inverse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368587} {:answer/id #uuid "23914e59-625c-5722-b1b7-881da7998491" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the definition of a basis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368588} {:answer/id #uuid "6bd627c0-fc65-5a27-844e-f8c51275ca1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bd627c0-fc65-5a27-844e-f8c51275ca1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368589} :answer-field/id #uuid "11c81fab-4e23-59d8-a36e-0ecad0d4726e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368585} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75c66bdd-6020-57b4-aeec-490f0e4fa183" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368591} {:answer/id #uuid "f7f6aa65-d5d0-5b53-9cfb-d6df63f7293e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368592} {:answer/id #uuid "5a59a05d-3a3e-52d0-af3c-da5690fcf97a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368593} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc58ef5-b356-5d39-90d9-b156a2c5bfd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a59a05d-3a3e-52d0-af3c-da5690fcf97a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368593} :answer-field/id #uuid "0dfbcea1-bc03-509d-bb99-ef587cec8af3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368590} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0f2e152-d682-5d24-9d25-f7c15a85a03a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368596} {:answer/id #uuid "dfa6381c-09e0-5214-9b20-ba64b8de33c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the properties of determinants" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368597} {:answer/id #uuid "4ec9f1c8-8b64-550e-8055-0dc1bb5ef5e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property of equality" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368598} {:answer/id #uuid "910026d1-a4e4-5476-bbcc-d94cb60ca252" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the definition of a basis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ec9f1c8-8b64-550e-8055-0dc1bb5ef5e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property of equality" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368598} :answer-field/id #uuid "577818a1-3045-5404-8f3b-938a82ba7462" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368595}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9fcd6208-dde9-5e8a-b2c1-ff9f0dade0db" :question/math-academy-id "q-336107" :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that every solution $x(t)$ can be written in the form $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c=[{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}]^{T}$ is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ be the columns of $Φ(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of solutions\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)$ can be written as $x(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $Φ(t)\\,c={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from {{field-1}} by the definition of a fundamental matrix.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines {{field-3}} by {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of the solution space for our system. Thus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the definition of a fundamental matrix.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Since ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are the columns of $Φ(t),$ we can write\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen by the definition of matrix multiplication,\n\n$$\nΦ(t)\\,c=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of matrix multiplication}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ In $\\text{L3}$ we have $x(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t),$ and in $\\text{L4}$ we have $Φ(t)c={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).$ Since both expressions are equal to the same quantity, the transitive property of equality gives $x(t)=Φ(t)c.$ Thus, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L3 and L4}$ by the $\\text{the transitive property of equality}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368600 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0aea7503-74d6-5ba4-9411-ee53e59512d0" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Properties of a Fundamental Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b162326b-1782-5055-a1e9-4d6dc7515a21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368602} {:answer/id #uuid "cadb21b9-a54a-5353-bc21-3a56069a7fcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ is diagonalizable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368603} {:answer/id #uuid "a57245f2-8594-5d66-9e55-22be0fd3ab70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368604} {:answer/id #uuid "3aa66913-49ff-59fc-8b02-77149d7119c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a57245f2-8594-5d66-9e55-22be0fd3ab70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368604} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb26a78f-ec86-57df-a4f6-824ccb1c2e96" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368601} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c57b44ce-9bdf-5a6e-a64d-d731d1a0512a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "factoring out $A$ on the left" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368607} {:answer/id #uuid "4b92f2e1-4048-54c9-91b6-75fa55751d74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by $A$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368608} {:answer/id #uuid "fada221d-18f9-5740-8505-e330e8db3179" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating each column" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368609} {:answer/id #uuid "a3d0f926-cad4-5dd7-b07e-7dd0e5277b9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "transposing the matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368610}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fada221d-18f9-5740-8505-e330e8db3179" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating each column" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368609} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab76daf2-5635-56e5-be3a-8a61f05ebd8d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368606} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb880c89-a496-5b76-9021-946b18b50257" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "factoring out $A$ on the left" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368612} {:answer/id #uuid "810c3167-f378-54b5-a21c-c25271b44561" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "transposing the matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368613} {:answer/id #uuid "7020615f-70fd-5981-b089-619da9914eed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating again" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368614} {:answer/id #uuid "b5149be5-f576-577e-b8a0-7c031368552f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ(t)$ to both sides" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb880c89-a496-5b76-9021-946b18b50257" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "factoring out $A$ on the left" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368612} :answer-field/id #uuid "66999d0e-3d88-58b0-a324-fbb375a9dfcc" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368611}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a12cf1e0-8187-51a8-afd1-8c77d727f77f" :question/math-academy-id "q-336309" :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that $Φ(t)$ satisfies the matrix differential equation ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A\\,Φ(t)$ is given below.\n\n*Hint: $[a,\\,b]$ denotes a matrix whose columns are vectors $a$ and $b.$*\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $Φ(t)=[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${x}_{2}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=[{x}_{1}^{′}(t),\\,{x}_{2}^{′}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=[A{x}_{1}(t),\\,A{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=AΦ(t)$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from the fact that $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix and line $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L5}$ by {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are solutions of the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$ Line $\\text{L1}$ identifies ${x}_{2}(t)$ as a column of $Φ(t),$ so ${x}_{2}(t)$ must satisfy the differential equation. In particular,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ follows from the fact that $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix and line $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Since $Φ(t)=[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)],$ the derivative of $Φ(t)$ is obtained by differentiating each column:\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=[{x}_{1}^{′}(t),\\,{x}_{2}^{′}(t)].\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{differentiating each column}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ We now factor the matrix $A$ on the left:\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=[A{x}_{1}(t),\\,A{x}_{2}(t)]=A[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by $\\text{factoring out }A\\text{ on the left}.$"}]}
